<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.3.1: Admin Selects Error/404: Page Not Found; Landin=
g Page for Creates Campaign Setup (Step 3.1)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to select the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</str=
ong> landing page template for my phishing campaign, apply filters to narro=
w down the templates, preview the selected template, and confirm the select=
ion, so that I can configure the appropriate landing page for the phishing =
campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case describes the process by which the Aspire Admin selects th=
e <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing page template for the =
phishing campaign. The Admin can filter landing page templates based on cri=
teria such as category and difficulty level, preview the selected template,=
 and confirm the landing page selection. The Admin can apply filters for ca=
tegories and difficulty levels and view a preview of the landing page templ=
ate before confirming the selection.</p>
<p>The Admin must choose the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> tem=
plate if they want to simulate the phishing scenario where a user encounter=
s an error page, typically used to engage users in phishing campaigns.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</s=
trong> landing page, applies filters, previews the template, and confirms t=
he selection.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the available landing page templates, =
applies filters, shows the preview of the selected template, and allows the=
 Admin to confirm their choice.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged into the platform and has access to the <strong>Create N=
ew Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is in the <strong>Landing Page Selection</strong> step.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>The system has available templates for <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found=
</strong> landing pages.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has the option to select between <strong>Landing Page</strong>=
, <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong>, or <strong>Custom Landing Pag=
e</strong>.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing page template is =
selected and confirmed for the phishing campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled to proceed to=
 the next step in the campaign creation.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Landing Page Selection</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Landing Page Selection</strong> step =
in the campaign creation wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> options, incl=
uding <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>Error/404 Page Not Found</stro=
ng>, and <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Search Template</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Admin can search the available Phishing Landing Page templates. placehol=
der: Search templates...<br>
Admin can search by keywords (e.g., "Holidays Offer").<br>
Admin can sort templates by popularity (Most to Least).<br>
Admin can search for templates using keywords.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Step 3: View Error/404: Page Not Found Templates</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the available landing page templates under <strong>Err=
or/404: Page Not Found Templates</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Templates are displayed with the template name, preview, and associated =
description (e.g., LinkedIn, Google Login, etc.).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Preview</strong> to view a preview of the la=
nding page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use Pagination to Navigate Between Pages</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can view the first page of 9 <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found=
</strong> After that it will show as pagination</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays pagination controls at the bottom of the campaign li=
st with the following options:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Previous</strong>: Navigate to the previous page.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Next</strong>: Navigate to the next page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The page number (e.g., "1", "2", "3", etc.) is highlighted to indicate t=
he current page.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Next</strong> or <strong>Previous</strong> to n=
avigate between pages of <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong>.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>The system updates the page content and displays the <strong>Error/404: =
Page Not Found </strong>from the selected page.</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Step 4: View Available Templates</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the available <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</stron=
g> landing page templates under <strong>Available Landing Page Templates</s=
trong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Templates are displayed with the template name, preview, and associated =
description (e.g., "Classic 404 Error," "Maintenance Page").</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Preview Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> <strong>Landi=
ng Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Preview</strong> button next to the <strong=
>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> template.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays a preview of the selected <strong>Error/404 Error Pa=
ge</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Example preview shows a 404 error message with a sad face icon and a "Go=
 to the homepage" button (as per the image provided).</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: Close Preview</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After reviewing the preview, the Admin can close the preview window by c=
licking the <strong>Close</strong> button.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 7: Select Landing Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After previewing and reviewing the landing page, the Admin clicks <stron=
g>Select</strong> to confirm the selection of the <strong>Error/404: Page N=
ot Found</strong> landing page template for the campaign.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 8: Proceed to Next Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Once the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing page is sele=
cted, the Admin can proceed to the next step by clicking <strong>Save &amp;=
 Continue</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page Type</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select the <strong>Error/404=
: Page Not Found</strong> landing page type.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid landing page type=
."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Available Landing Page Templates</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory after applying filter=
s.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select a valid <strong>Error=
/404: Page Not Found</strong> template from the list.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a 404 error page template=
."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preview</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin must preview the selected template befo=
re confirming.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Admin must click <strong>Preview</strong> t=
o view the template before selecting it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please preview the selected template be=
fore proceeding."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"ad=
d556ff-d322-484d-80cf-1b9208e84a38" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must choose a <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing p=
age type before selecting a template.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter available landing page templates based on <strong>Categ=
ory</strong> and <strong>Difficulty Level</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must <strong>Preview</strong> the selected template before confirm=
ing the selection.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Preview</strong> button must show an accurate representation=
 of the selected 404 landing page.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> templat=
e for campaigns simulating error pages.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-6</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must apply <strong>Landing Page Filters</strong> to narrow down av=
ailable templates by category and difficulty.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-7</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must confirm their selection by clicking <strong>Select</strong>.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"97=
4d22fb-4aac-4ae8-a9f7-285794e70ef6" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing =
page type.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Error/</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>404: Page Not Found</strong> is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing=
 page template by clicking <strong>Preview</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>A preview of the 404 error page is displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can close the preview window by clicking <strong>Close</strong>.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview window closes and returns to the template list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can confirm the selection by clicking <strong>Select</strong>.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The selected 404 landing page template is confirmed and saved.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can proceed to the next step after confirming the landing page sel=
ection.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled after selection.<=
/p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview a <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> landing p=
age template before selecting it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview displays an accurate representation of the template.</p></td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select a <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> template =
before proceeding.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is disabled until a temp=
late is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select <strong>Error/404 Page Not Found</strong> from the avai=
lable templates and apply them to the campaign.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>404 Page Not Found</strong> is correctly selected and applied.</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select <strong>Classic 404 Error Page</strong> template.</p></=
td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select the <strong>Classic 404 Error Page</strong> template fr=
om the available list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view and interact with the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</=
strong> preview in real-time.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The 404 error page template reflects any updates immediately.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong> type, an=
d the preview accurately reflects the template=E2=80=99s content.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Preview is an exact match for the selected 404 error template.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin is able to view the <strong>Go to the homepage</strong> button in =
the preview.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Go to the homepage</strong> button is visible and functional=
 in the preview.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can confirm the landing page selection without needing to make fur=
ther modifications.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Once confirmed, the template is saved and ready for the next step.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view a valid error message if they try to proceed without sele=
cting a template.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Error message appears if no template is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can confirm their selection of the <strong>Error/404: Page Not Fou=
nd</strong> template only after previewing it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Select</strong> button is only enabled after previewing the =
landing page.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> if required.</p></=
td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom landing page option is available for selection.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page Type</strong>: Admin must select one of the three a=
vailable landing page types (<strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>404 Pag=
e Not Found</strong>, <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preview</strong>: Admin can preview the landing page by clicking=
 the <strong>Preview</strong> button. The system ensures that the preview i=
s accurate and matches the selected template.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Integrity</strong>: All landing page selections and preview=
s are securely stored. Only authorized Admins can modify landing page templ=
ates.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audit Logs</strong>: The system logs all actions related to temp=
late selection and filtering for audit purposes.</p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
